<!doctype html>
<html>
<head>
<title>A theme of custom properties: components whose colours and sizes come from custom properties with fallbacks, in the theme on the root (page 99 draws the same switched by a class that redeclares them)</title>
<style>
  :root {
    --page: #f6f2ea;
    --surface: #e0d8c8;
    --ink: #2f3542;
    --accent: #3a7a4a;
    --accent-soft: #a8c8b0;
    --warn: #a0522d;
    --space: 8px;
    --bar: 40px;
    --edge: 2px;
    --progress: 60;
  }
  /* The other theme, redeclaring every property but one, whose fallback
     is then used; and its spacing larger. */
  .alt {
    --page: #1e1e2e;
    --surface: #313244;
    --ink: #cdd6f4;
    --accent: #89b4fa;
    --accent-soft: #45475a;
    --warn: unset;
    --space: 12px;
    --bar: 48px;
    --edge: 4px;
    --progress: 35;
  }
  html { background-color: var(--page); }
  body { margin: 0; }

  .toolbar { display: flex; gap: var(--space); height: var(--bar); padding: 0 var(--space); align-items: cent